  sanctions='AI sanctions: track limits, cut corners, jump start, pit lane, wrong way, penalties and giving a place back.',
  overlay='In-game overlay, set like the SuperHUD ones: position and size (unlock, drag, bottom right corner), background and opacities, content (session info, flag explanations, race summary) and Assetto Corsa displays taken over. Shared by every session.',
  general='Pace, aggression, caution and differences between drivers.',
  yield='When and how an AI lets a faster car behind through (track day, practice, qualifying). In the race, its offset, hold and confirmation settings are also used for blue flags, faster classes and overtaking; when the section is off, their default values apply.',
  blue='Blue flags: priority to the cars lapping.',
  flash='Player headlight flashes and AI-to-AI headlight flashes.',
  overtake='Preparing, pulling out, margins and completing overtakes; slipstream and defending.',
  lateral='Speed, smoothing and limits of lateral movement, anti-weaving.',
  human='Driver personality: reactions, awareness, pace and line variations, focus, driving mistakes.',
  start='Standing starts of races: delay, caution and settling time.',
  accidents='Stopped, crashed, spinning or wrong-way cars: avoidance, stopping the AI involved, yellow zone.',
  rules='Championship rules (base, Formula 1, GT, Endurance), neutralisations, red flag, Formula 1 2026, DRS and beeps, BoP and classes. Pit stops and Safety Car: under their own title, on the left.',
  endurance='Endurance layer, multi-class and class patterns.',
  weather='Adapting pace and tyres to the rain.',
  lights='Our flags on the FIA light panels of equipped tracks: colours, durations and sessions.',
  traffic='Traffic spacing on a track day.',
  globals='Options shared by all profiles: level mode, grip, braking, lateral occupancy, personality seed. Each profile only applies them if its Global options section is on.',
 },
 sections={
  strategy='Applies the AI strategy to the profile shown (it acts in the race only). Unticked: stops left to the racing rules and to AC, no failures.',
  sanctions='Applies the AI sanctions to the profile shown (practice, qualifying and race). Unticked: no such sanctions for the AI.',
  general='Applies the settings of this section to the profile shown. Off: native level, aggression and caution, with no differences between drivers.',
  yield='Applies the yielding settings to the profile shown. Off: no standard yielding and no reaction to pressure.',
  blue='Applies blue flags to the profile shown. Off: no yielding to the cars lapping.',
  flash='Applies headlight flashes to the profile shown. Off: your flashes are ignored and the AI do not flash each other.',
  overtake='Applies overtaking to the profile shown. Off: no commanded overtakes, no defending, no slipstream.',
  lateral='Applies the line settings to the profile shown. Off: the default values of the profile.',
  human='Applies the driver personalities to the profile shown. Off: neutral drivers, with no variation in pace, line or focus, and no driving mistakes.',
  start='Applies the start procedure to the profile shown (Race). Off: no start delay and no settling time.',
  accidents='Applies accident handling to the profile shown. Off: no avoidance, no stopping of crashed AI, no yellow zone, no penalties; the flag panel and messages stay available for neutralisations and the red flag as long as the racing rules are on.',
  rules='Applies the racing rules to the profile shown. Off: no sporting rules (no neutralisation, red flag, mandatory stop, Overtake Mode, BoP, Pro-Am, predictable slower class, nor DRS disabled or opened by the app).',
  endurance='Applies the Endurance layer and the classes to the profile shown. Off: a single class.',
  weather='Applies the weather adaptation to the profile shown. Off: pace and tyres unchanged in the rain.',
  traffic='Applies spacing to the profile shown; it only acts on a Track day.',
  lights='Applies the track light panels to the profile shown. Unticked: the AC flag is left as it is in this session type.',
  globals='Applies the global options (values shared by all profiles) to the profile shown. Off: conservative default values for this profile.',
 },
 profiles={
  H='Hotlap: profile for sessions without AI (hotlap, time attack, drift, drag), chosen automatically by the detection. Its settings are its own: the Track day profile is no longer affected by these sessions. By default only the racing rules are on (Racing rules tab), with the base rules: flag panel and messages, DRS beep and badge; penalties and championship rules do not apply.',
  J='Track day: Touristenfahrten-style traffic, standard yielding to the right, AI spacing. Clicking shows this profile so you can view or edit it. With the automatic profile, the detected session always chooses the profile used in game; without it, this profile becomes the one in use.',
  P='Practice: standalone or race-weekend practice sessions; yielding to faster cars, practice pace. Clicking shows this profile so you can view or edit it. With the automatic profile, the detected session always chooses the profile used in game; without it, this profile becomes the one in use.',
  Q='Qualifying: slow AI move clearly out of the way of a flying lap. Clicking shows this profile so you can view or edit it. With the automatic profile, the detected session always chooses the profile used in game; without it, this profile becomes the one in use.',
  C='Race: no standard yielding, blue flags, overtaking and defending, start, racing rules. Clicking shows this profile so you can view or edit it. With the automatic profile, the detected session always chooses the profile used in game; without it, this profile becomes the one in use.',
 },
 presets={
  J='Nordschleife Touristenfahrten preset, applied to the Track day profile: dense traffic, yielding to the right, headlight flashes, spacing, accidents and weather.',
  P='Free practice preset, applied to the Practice profile: practice pace (97%), calmer drivers, yielding to faster cars, accidents and weather.',
  Q='Flying-lap qualifying preset, applied to the Qualifying profile: slow AI move clearly out of the way of a fast lap.',
  C='Realistic race preset, applied to the Race profile: blue flags, overtaking on the automatic side, defending, careful start, accidents and weather. It also sets the championship rules (base rules: mandatory stop, Safety Car, rule set) for the whole weekend (Practice, Qualifying and Race); only your preferences and class patterns are kept.',
  E='Multi-class endurance preset, applied to the Race profile (or Track day if that is the profile shown): classes, Endurance layer, lapses in focus. Applied to the Race profile, it also sets the Endurance rules for Practice, Qualifying and Race.',
 },
 rules={
  base='Common base rules: no change of direction under braking, local yellow zone (double yellow at delta time +15%), Safety Car if the incident escalates, red flag on a pile-up with a real restart, no mandatory stop.',
  F1='Formula 1 2025: VSC on a major incident (VSC ending announced), Safety Car if the incident escalates, one stop with a change of dry compound (before 95% of the race, unless the race is wet), tyres changed under a red flag, DRS after one lap by the leader at the start and after a Safety Car or a red flag, disabled in the rain and under flags.',
  F1_2026='Formula 1 2026: as in 2025, but without DRS: active aero with no wait (AC’s DRS, disabled in the rain and under flags) and Overtake Mode, detected once per lap within one second, for the straights of the next lap.',
  GT='GT World Challenge Sprint: FCY at the equivalent of 80 km/h (delta +150%), Safety Car if the incident escalates, pits open under FCY (SRO regulations), one mandatory stop between 25 and 35 minutes of a one-hour race (42 to 58%) with no minimum time, no work on the cars under a red flag, BoP and Pro-Am ratings.',
  Endurance='Endurance (WEC): FCY at the equivalent of 80 km/h (delta +150%), Safety Car if the incident escalates, 80 km/h Slow Zone under double yellow, pit lane closed under FCY and for three Safety Car laps, stints of 50 min at most (approximation), free refuelling as the race goes on (at every end of stint and whenever the tank requires it), new tyres and repairs at every stop, BoP, Pro-Am ratings, slower class with a predictable line.',
 },
 ui={
  -- Racing 26 redesign (Beta 1.35).
  warnLink='Opens the section concerned.',bannerAction='Quick action: enables the app again, resumes after panic or opens diagnostics.',
  patternClear='Clears this pattern (frees the row).',performance='Cost of the app AI loop, interface drawing excluded: mean and maximum over the latest frames.',
  overlayRecenter='Puts the overlay back at its automatic position (centred, at the top of the screen) and back to its original size (1.00x).',
  version='Installed app version. Updates, release notes and roll back: Diagnostic tab.',
  status='Engine state: active when the app drives the AI in this session, with the profile in use. The line below gives the reason for a stop (online session, replay, pause, panic, no section on…).',
  tab_home='Home: profile shown and edited, detected session, built-in presets (one click sets the profile concerned) and custom presets, live status and things to check.',
  mandatoryStop='Mandatory stop in the race, set for Practice, Qualifying and Race at once: on, at least one pit stop to make within the set window (a single stop is required; everyone, AI and player alike, may then make as many stops as their strategy needs); off, no stop imposed. The F1 2025, F1 2026 and GT rules switch it on, the base and Endurance rules leave it off (in Endurance, the 50 min maximum stint forces the stops); one click adds or removes it with any rule set, which stays highlighted. The toggle shows the state of the Race profile; on a Track day and in Hotlap, where none of this applies, it stays off. A Practice, Qualifying or Race preset also sets it for the whole weekend.',
  safetySwitch='Safety Car escalation, set for Practice, Qualifying and Race at once: in the race, if the incident escalates (at least 2 cars stopped on track, or a long recovery), the Safety Car is deployed, after a VSC, an FCY or the local yellow zone. On by default with every rule set (F1 2025, F1 2026, GT, Endurance and base rules); one click removes or adds it, and the rule set stays highlighted. Default model: the Ferrari 458 Italia Stage 3 from the base game, to add to the grid in Content Manager; click the “Safety Car” title to pick another one. The toggle shows the state of the Race profile; on a Track day and in Hotlap, where none of this applies, it stays off. A Practice, Qualifying or Race preset also sets it for the whole weekend.',
  rulesViewAll='Shows on the right the racing rules of the profile shown, except pit stops and the Safety Car (under their own title). Only the switch turns the rules on or off.',
  rulesViewStops='Shows on the right the race pit stop settings: number of stops, window, tyres, minimum time, maximum stint, fuel, pit lane closed. Only the switch turns the mandatory stop on or off.',
  rulesViewSafety='Shows on the right the Safety Car settings: escalation, speed on track and choice of the model on the grid. Only the switch turns the Safety Car on or off.',
  rulesReset='Resets the racing rules of Practice, Qualifying and Race to the values of the highlighted rule set (or the closest one if you edited it on the right), mandatory stop and Safety Car included. Your preferences (DRS beep and panel, volume, pit window message) and the Safety Car model are kept.',
  sectionReset='Resets every setting of this section to the defaults of the profile shown (like a right-click on a setting). Your display preferences, the class patterns and the settings set by the rule set are kept. Global options: only the ones of this tab, never the measured lateral direction nor the Safety Car.',
  tab_rules='Racing rules: on the left, three rows (racing rules on, mandatory stop in the race, Safety Car) whose title shows the settings on the right and whose switch turns the option on or off, then the championship rule sets (base, F1 2025, F1 2026, GT, Endurance), applied together to Practice, Qualifying and Race, and the reset. Right-click a setting: the default value of the profile.',
  tab_settings='Settings: choose a section in the list; its toggle switches it on or off for the profile shown. Right-click a setting: the default value of the profile.',
  tab_diagnostic='Diagnostics: available CSP functions, sign calibration, headlight flashes, zones, session log, table of the AI driven, performance and event log.',
  enabled='Switches the whole app on or off: when off, the AI are fully native again.',
  auto='Chooses the profile from the detected session (track day, practice, qualifying or race), race weekends included. Off: the profile chosen by hand stays active.',
  panic='Immediately stops all of the app’s commands: the AI are native again until you resume.',
  language='Interface language: French (FR) or English (EN). Immediately changes the settings window, the tooltips, the flag panel and the on-screen messages; the choice is saved. The session log stays in French.',
  resume='Resumes the commands after a panic, from the current line of the AI.',
  presetBySession='On (default): as soon as a session is detected (automatic profile), its built-in preset is applied and lit: Free practice in practice, Qualifying flying lap in qualifying, Realistic race in the race, Nordschleife Touristenfahrten on a track day (the Nordschleife included). Another built-in preset you chose for this profile (Multi-class endurance) is kept; a personal preset loaded into this profile is never replaced. Your championship rules (rule set, mandatory stop, Safety Car), preferences and class patterns are kept. Your changes during the session stay until the next session. Off: the recommended preset is only applied to a profile never set, as before.',
  restore='Resets every value of the profile shown to its default. Sections that are on stay on; the chosen racing rules (F1 2025, F1 2026, GT, Endurance...), your preferences (panel, messages, HUD flag, DRS and delta beeps, volume) and your class patterns are kept.',
  reroll='Draws a new seed: new personalities for all the AI.',
  customPreset='Loads this custom preset into its profile (saved values and global options).',
  deletePreset='Permanently deletes this custom preset.',
  presetName='Name of the custom preset to save: 64 bytes at most (an accented letter counts as two).',
  savePreset='Saves the profile shown and the global options under this name (16 presets at most); an existing name is replaced.',
  patterns='Class patterns: part of the car folder name followed by its class (1 = fastest), for example “lmp1:1,gt3:2”. They take priority over the automatic classification by pace.',
  patternRows='Shows the eight pattern and class pairs as separate fields.',
  patternRow='Part of the car folder name (letters, digits, hyphen or underscore); left empty, the row is ignored.',
  classRow='Class given to cars whose folder contains this pattern: 1 = fastest, 4 = slowest.',
  safetyClear='Removes the Safety Car: under the “Safety Car” neutralisation, an FCY is used instead.',
  safetyModel='Exact name of the car folder in content/cars. The car must be on the grid in Content Manager.',
  safetyFilter='Filters the list of installed cars by part of their name (as Content Manager shows it) or of their folder.',
  safetyPick='Picks the Safety Car from all installed cars, listed as “name (folder)”; then add it to the grid in Content Manager.',
  journal='Writes the session log to Documents/Assetto Corsa/logs (AdvancedIA.log, three older ones kept): sessions, incidents, a summary every minute.',
  apiList='Shows the list of AI functions exposed by this CSP.',
  calibrate='Reruns the calibration of the left/right reference on two isolated AI cars on a straight. Lateral manoeuvres wait for the confirmation.',
  learn='For 6 s, give several short headlight flashes: the app learns which signal of your car is the flash.',
  markStart='Marks the start of a no-manoeuvre zone at the position of your car.',
  markEnd='Marks the end of the zone at the position of your car: no yielding or overtaking will be commanded there.',
  export='Copies the zones to the clipboard, to paste into tracks/<id>.lua; no track file is changed.',
  zoneCount='No-manoeuvre zones of this track: loaded from tracks/<id>.lua or marked during the session. The copy button exports them to the clipboard; no track file is changed.',
  filter='Changes the level of the messages shown: all, errors, warnings, information or details.',
  -- Update from GitHub (Beta 1.33).
  updateInstall='Installs the new version in one click: download from GitHub, check of the SHA-256 digest and of the package contents, backup of the current version, then the app hands the AI back to AC and restarts. Your settings, profiles and presets are kept.',
  updateDriving='Updating is possible only when stopped: pits, pause or menu.',
  updateCancel='Cancels the download in progress; nothing has been changed yet.',
  updateCheck='Asks GitHub for the latest published version (one request). Nothing is downloaded or installed until you click Update.',
  updateNotes='Opens the release page on GitHub in your browser.',
  updateRollback='Puts back the version saved before the last update, then the app restarts. Your settings are kept.',
  updateToggle='At launch, a single request to GitHub (api.github.com) to know whether a newer version exists; no personal data is sent. Untick to never contact GitHub.',
 },
}
